  "reason": "The records provide several relevant ingredients: R3 demonstrates combined high-pressure/high-temperature treatment in a closely related HEA; the other pressure studies establish pressure-driven structural transformations involving stacking faults, dislocations, and twinning; R2, R10, and R16 establish the FCC/B2 lamellar architecture and soft-FCC/hard-B2 deformation behavior of closely matching eutectic alloys; and R4 shows that coherent nanoscale structures can form in Al0.75CoCrFeNi. The nanowire studies also identify synergistic dislocation, stacking-fault, twinning, and transformation mechanisms. However, no record teaches that HPHT treatment of the Al0.7CoCrFeNi eutectic will convert incoherent lamellae into a hierarchical pattern with coherent FCC/B2 interfaces, nor that those interfaces will promote preferential FCC-to-B2 dislocation transfer and suppress interfacial cracking. Combining the scattered clues would therefore require a substantial new microstructural-design idea."
